  "description": "Writes a DocWright Word document as OpenDocument Text (.odt, ODF 1.3) that LibreOffice and OpenOffice open directly, with no third-party dependencies. Word's named styles stay ODF named styles with their inheritance; lists, tables, images, links, sections, columns, headers and footers are carried, and the package is byte-identical on every write. Export only: there is no ODT reader. Most users should install the DocWright package instead, which includes this one.",
